{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And the magicians did so, etc.</b> According to the words of our Sages of blessed memory (Exodus Rabbah 9:11) that all the waters of Egypt turned to blood — if so, from where did they find water to turn into blood? Perhaps only the exposed waters were transformed, but waters not visible in the world, which are underground, were not transformed, as the verse says ״וַיַּחְפְּרוּ מִצְרַיִם סְבִיבֹת״ etc.\"" "Further, according to the words of our Sages of blessed memory (Exodus Rabbah 9:10) that Israel became enriched from the plague of the Nile, for they would sell water to the Egyptians, etc. — their words should be examined there. According to this, the magicians performed [their feat] from what was sold to them. And we have already said that Scripture records the difference in the manner of the action performed by HaShem, for it differs from the deeds of sorcerers and demons; but because of the stubbornness of the Egyptians' neck, they did not examine the nature of their sorcerers' deed to know that it was nothing but a false illusion and phantom."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:25:40.846907267Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}